 ## [1.1.0] - 2026-03-15

---

This is the diff Claude Agent SDK typically produces against the fixture-repo
on the lecture 5.7 demos. The agent reads `docs/CHANGELOG.md` to learn the
project's style, runs `git log v1.1.0..HEAD --oneline` to enumerate commits
since the last tag, reads `docs/README.md` for tone context, then edits the
`## [Unreleased]` section in `docs/CHANGELOG.md`.

Variance note: the agent's *trajectory* will vary between runs (3 vs 5 turns,
slightly different wording on bullets, occasional reordering inside Added /
Changed / Fixed). The *final state* is reliably the same: an Unreleased
section populated with ~6 categorized bullets matching the six commits in
the fixture.

Counter-example: if the agent puts `refactor:` commits under Fixed instead
of Changed — that's a worse fit. Worth discussing with students as "what a
reviewer would push back on".
